From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: honour an opp-suspend OPP as the non-S2RAM memory floor

On OPP platforms qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() drops the OPP to NULL for
non-S2RAM suspend, voting average/peak bandwidth of 0/0 on the PCIe
memory path. These OPP votes are the PCIe controller's only DDR/LLCC
contribution to the RPMh sleep set; with no PCIe memory-path sleep vote
the SM8550 AOP never hands control back once the CPU cluster collapses
in s2idle, and the device hard resets on wake.

Select an OPP marked opp-suspend for non-S2RAM suspend, as modeled by
the OPP core, and keep the drop to NULL when the DT defines no suspend
OPP.

Non-obvious choices:
- Do not populate pcie->icc_mem as an alternative on OPP platforms:
  qcom_pcie_icc_opp_update() takes the icc_mem branch when that handle
  is present, bypassing OPP updates and pinning the memory-path vote at
  its probe-time maximum.
- The helper is guarded on pm_suspend_target_state so S2RAM still drops
  the OPP entirely; its call sites run for every system-sleep target.
- The suspend OPP is resolved with dev_pm_opp_get_suspend_opp_freq()
  plus dev_pm_opp_find_freq_exact(); the synthetic opp-hz in the
  companion DT keeps that frequency unique within the table.

The root-cause analysis and the opp-suspend approach come from Luke
Johnson's fix for this hardware in thorch
(packages/linux-thorch/patches/0220-PCI-qcom-use-suspend-opp-for-non-s2ram.patch);
this is an independent implementation for Linux 7.2.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/c04b39f9fe97df042f42909d75819ccc7985f596/packages/kernel/patches/0513-PCI-qcom-honour-an-opp-suspend-opp-as-the-non-s2ram-memory-floor.patch
Link: https://github.com/noahcdls/armada/blob/c10ea8511b6af48a7e05bc5a9dfb2199af227e51/packages/kernel/patches/0543-PCI-qcom-let-the-suspend-opp-floor-be-skipped-for-debugging.patch
(armada 0513; earliest history in armada is its import from
armada-packages in commit 956bd2c73e61 by Radical, whose date is used
above; 0543 "PCI: qcom: let the suspend OPP floor be skipped for
debugging" from armada-os PR #722)

Local changes (nixos-android-devices): regenerated against Linux 7.3 with
git headers; folds in armada 0543, the writable module parameter
pcie_qcom.suspend_opp_floor (default Y; N restores the upstream drop to
NULL) so the floor can be A/B tested without a rebuild.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2337,6 +2337,41 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* Debug knob: drop the suspend OPP floor to reproduce the s2idle hang. */
+static bool suspend_opp_floor = true;
+module_param(suspend_opp_floor, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend_opp_floor,
+		 "Keep the DT suspend OPP during s2idle (default: Y)");
+
+/*
+ * Use the DT suspend OPP to retain the PCIe DDR/LLCC sleep-set votes
+ * during s2idle. Suspend-to-RAM tears the link down and keeps dropping
+ * the OPP.
+ */
+static int qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
+{
+	struct device *dev = pcie->pci->dev;
+	struct dev_pm_opp *opp;
+	unsigned long freq;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM || !suspend_opp_floor)
+		return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
+
+	freq = dev_pm_opp_get_suspend_opp_freq(dev);
+	if (!freq)
+		return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
+
+	opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_exact(dev, freq, true);
+	if (IS_ERR(opp))
+		return PTR_ERR(opp);
+
+	ret = dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, opp);
+	dev_pm_opp_put(opp);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_pcie *pcie;
@@ -2359,8 +2394,11 @@
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
 
-		if (pcie->use_pm_opp)
-			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(pcie->pci->dev, NULL);
+		if (pcie->use_pm_opp) {
+			ret = qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(pcie);
+			if (ret)
+				dev_err(dev, "Failed to set suspend OPP: %d\n", ret);
+		}
 	} else {
 		/*
 		 * Set minimum bandwidth required to keep data path
@@ -2388,8 +2426,12 @@
 				dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n",
 					ret);
 
-			if (pcie->use_pm_opp)
-				dev_pm_opp_set_opp(pcie->pci->dev, NULL);
+			if (pcie->use_pm_opp) {
+				ret = qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(pcie);
+				if (ret)
+					dev_err(dev, "Failed to set suspend OPP: %d\n",
+						ret);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 	return ret;
